course: dictionary
lesson: 10147
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The clues in the sentence tell you which meaning the writer chose. «The throne was made of gold.» Here the throne is a seat, because you can make a seat out of gold.
explain: Now read «He came to the throne after his father died.» A chair cannot be "come to", so this throne means the position of being king or queen. The words around it give the clue.
explain: Sometimes a word is used as a joke. People call the toilet «the throne», which is informal and playful. Only use this joke meaning when the people talking are joking, and check the words around it.
fact: A throne is a special chair that a king, queen or ruler sits on at ceremonies.
fact: «The throne» can also mean the position and power of a king or queen, as in «to come to the throne».
fact: «Heir to the throne» means the person who will become the next ruler.
fact: As an informal joke, «the throne» means the toilet.
fact: When a word has more than one meaning, read the words around it to find the right one.
exercise: «The king sat on his golden throne.» What is a throne? | * A special chair for a king, queen or ruler | A tall tower in a castle | A type of crown | A bed with velvet curtains
exercise: «The prince was heir to the throne.» What does "the throne" mean here? | A seat in the palace kitchen | A song sung at weddings | * The power and position of a king or queen | A list of royal names
exercise: People joke and call the toilet "the throne". Why is that funny? | It is the name of a famous castle | * It is an informal joke, because a toilet is not a royal seat | It is a science word | It means a king lives there
test: «King Edward VII was on the throne in 1908.» What does "on the throne" mean? | He was sitting on a chair in the garden | He was very old | He was a farmer | * He was the ruler at that time
test: «To come to the throne» means what? | * To become the ruler | To climb up a hill | To sit down for dinner | To be made into a statue
exam: Ella reads «the heir to the throne» and thinks of a chair. Which clue shows the word means power, not a seat? | The word throne has five letters | The word heir, which sounds like air | * The word heir, which means someone who will rule next | The word the, which is very common
